@startuml student-message-turn
title A student message: the agent is invoked twice, and the VerifyShield sits between the two calls

' High level. Detail lives in web/server/turn/handle-turn.ts (answerMessage), agents/ and verify-shield/decide.ts.
' The Deskmate (Mai) follows the same pattern with its own two moves; it is left out to keep the picture short.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 14
autonumber

actor Student
participant "Browser" as Browser
participant "Turn\n(server)" as Turn
participant "Teacher\n(agents)" as Teacher
participant "Language\nmodel" as LM
participant "VerifyShield\n(decide)" as Shield

Student -> Browser : types any message
Browser -> Turn : POST /turn { message }

Turn -> Turn : load what the student knows\n(mastery, which modules are open)\nbuild the Teacher's prompt:\nroadmap, materials, exercise, code, conversation

== Call 1: choose a move (no words yet) ==
Turn -> Teacher : propose(context)
Teacher -> LM : instructions: "propose one move, or none"\n+ prompt
LM --> Teacher : move, for example\n{ type: explain_concept, scope: loops }\nor null
Teacher --> Turn : proposed move

== Rule: the VerifyShield approves or changes the move ==
Turn -> Shield : decide(move, what the student knows)
alt allowed
  Shield --> Turn : allow (the move as proposed)
else wrong role, or module closed, or out of course
  Shield --> Turn : block, or downgrade to redirect_to_module
end
Turn -> Turn : write the proposal and the verdict to the decision log

== Call 2: write the paragraph for the approved move ==
alt allow
  Turn -> Teacher : render(context, approved move)
  Teacher -> LM : instructions: "write only the message for the approved move"\n+ the same prompt + "Approved move: explain_concept"
  LM --> Teacher : paragraph, word by word
  Teacher --> Turn : text
  Turn --> Browser : stream the paragraph
else downgrade to redirect_to_module
  Turn --> Browser : fixed redirect text from the course\n(the model is not called a second time)
else block, or no proposal
  Turn --> Browser : nothing from the Teacher
end
Browser --> Student : the paragraph appears

Turn --> Browser : final state: messages, roadmap,\nand a trace of proposal and verdict

note over Turn, Shield
  The model never writes words the VerifyShield has not approved.
  Call 1 answers "what kind of move?". Call 2 answers "what do I say?".
end note
@enduml
